/-!
# Generating families on manifolds

A real function `S(q, a)` on `M × A`, where `M` is a manifold and the *auxiliary variables* `a`
range over a real normed space `A`, is a **generating family** over `M`. Its *fibre derivative* is
the differential of `S(q, ·)`,

`∂_a S : M × A → A'`, `(q, a) ↦ d_a S(q, a)`

(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.familyFiberDeriv`). It is `C^m` when `S` is `C^(m+1)`, for any `C¹`
manifold `M`, possibly with boundary or corners, and any normed space `A`
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.contMDiff_familyFiberDeriv`); its differential is computed below on a
boundaryless `C²` manifold `M`. Its *fibre-critical set* is the zero set
`Σ_S = {(q, a) | ∂_a S(q, a) = 0}`, and the source projection
`ι_S (q, a) = (q, d_q S(q, a))` of the cotangent relation generated by `S`
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.generatingSource`) maps it to `T*M`. This file is the manifold version of
the generating families on normed spaces, `TauCeti.cotangentFamilyFiberDeriv` and
`TauCeti.isLagrangianImmersion_cotangentGeneratingSource_comp_coe`.

The family is *transverse* when `0` is a regular value of `∂_a S`. From here on `S` is smooth, `M`
is a smooth boundaryless manifold, and `M` and `A` are finite-dimensional. For a transverse family,
`Σ_S` is a regular level of `∂_a S`, so with the atlas of `TauCeti.regularLevelChartedSpace`
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.familyCriticalSetChartedSpace`) it is a smooth manifold of the dimension
of `M` (`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.isManifold_familyCriticalSet`), smoothly embedded in `M × A`, with
tangent spaces the kernels of the differential of `∂_a S`
(`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.range_mfderiv_coe_familyCriticalSet`). With the conventions
`λ(v) = p(dπ v)` and `ω = -dλ` of `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.liouvilleForm` and
`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.symplecticForm`:

* **Exactness.** `ι_S` pulls `λ` back along the inclusion of `Σ_S` to the differential of the
  restriction of `S` (`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.mpullback_generatingSource_comp_coe_liouvilleForm`),
  since `dS = d_q S + ∂_a S` and the second summand vanishes on `Σ_S`. Hence `ι_S` pulls `ω` back
  to `-d(dS) = 0` there, without computing second derivatives of `S`.
* **Immersion.** The differential of `∂_a S` at `(q, a)` sends `(w, c)` to
  `b ↦ d_a (d_q S)(b)(w) + D²_a S(c, b)`, the mixed Hessian of `S` plus the second derivative of
  `S(q, ·)` (`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.mvfderiv_familyFiberDeriv_apply`). If a tangent vector of
  `Σ_S` is killed by the differential of `ι_S`, its base component vanishes, and its auxiliary
  component `b` is killed by the mixed Hessian and lies in the kernel of the differential of
  `∂_a S`. By the symmetry of second derivatives every covector in the range of that differential
  then vanishes on `b`, and transversality makes this range all of `A'`, so `b = 0`.

Therefore `ι_S` restricted to `Σ_S` is an exact Lagrangian map with primitive the restriction of
`S` (`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.isExactLagrangianMap_generatingSource_comp_coe`) and a Lagrangian
immersion into `T*M` (`TauCeti.CotangentBundle.isLagrangianImmersion_generatingSource_comp_coe`).
Its image need not be embedded: distinct critical points with the same image under `ι_S` give
self-intersections.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.familyFiberDeriv S`: the fibre derivative `∂_a S` of a generating family.
* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.familyCriticalSetChartedSpace`: the charted-space structure on the
  fibre-critical set of a smooth transverse generating family.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.isManifold_familyCriticalSet`: the fibre-critical set of a smooth
  transverse generating family is a manifold of the dimension of `M`.
* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.isExactLagrangianMap_generatingSource_comp_coe`: the fibre-critical set
  maps to `T*M` by `ι_S` as an exact Lagrangian map with primitive the restriction of `S`.
* `TauCeti.CotangentBundle.isLagrangianImmersion_generatingSource_comp_coe`: this map is a
  Lagrangian immersion.

## References

* L. Hörmander, *Fourier integral operators. I*, Acta Math. 127 (1971), 79–183, Section 3.1, for
  the Lagrangian defined by a nondegenerate phase function.
* A. Weinstein, *Lectures on Symplectic Manifolds*, CBMS Regional Conference Series in
  Mathematics 29, AMS, 1977, for generating families (Morse families).
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Bundle Manifold Module
open scoped Manifold ContDiff

namespace TauCeti.CotangentBundle

variable {M A : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup A] [NormedSpace ℝ A] {S : M × A → ℝ}

/-! ### The fibre derivative -/

/-- The **fibre derivative** `∂_a S(q, a)` of a generating family `S : M × A → ℝ` in its
auxiliary variables `a ∈ A`: the differential at `a` of `S(q, ·)`. -/
def familyFiberDeriv (S : M × A → ℝ) (x : M × A) : StrongDual ℝ A :=
  mvfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, A) (fun a ↦ S (x.1, a)) x.2

/-- The fibre derivative is the vector-valued differential of `S(q, ·)`. -/
theorem familyFiberDeriv_def (S : M × A → ℝ) (x : M × A) :
    familyFiberDeriv S x = mvfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, A) (fun a ↦ S (x.1, a)) x.2 :=
  (rfl)

/-- The fibre derivative is the Fréchet derivative of `S(q, ·)`. -/
theorem familyFiberDeriv_eq_fderiv (S : M × A → ℝ) (x : M × A) :
    familyFiberDeriv S x = fderiv ℝ (fun a ↦ S (x.1, a)) x.2 := by
  ext b
  exact mvfderiv_eq_fderiv_apply _ _ b

@[simp]
theorem familyFiberDeriv_apply (S : M × A → ℝ) (x : M × A) (b : A) :
    familyFiberDeriv S x b = fderiv ℝ (fun a ↦ S (x.1, a)) x.2 b := by
  rw [familyFiberDeriv_eq_fderiv]

/-- The fibre derivative of `S` is the negated covector of the target projection of the cotangent
relation generated by `S`. -/
theorem familyFiberDeriv_eq_neg_generatingTarget_snd (S : M × A → ℝ) (x : M × A) :
    familyFiberDeriv S x = -(generatingTarget 𝓘(ℝ, A) S x).2 := by
  ext b
  exact (neg_neg _).symm.trans (congrArg Neg.neg
    (DFunLike.congr_fun (generatingTarget_snd (J := 𝓘(ℝ, A)) (S := S) x) b).symm)

variable {E H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [TopologicalSpace H]
  {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H} [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H M]

/-- The fibre derivative of a generating family which is `C^n` at `x` is `C^m` at `x` when
`m + 1 ≤ n`. -/
theorem contMDiffAt_familyFiberDeriv [IsManifold I 1 M] {m n : WithTop ℕ∞} {x : M × A}
    (hS : ContMDiffAt (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) 𝓘(ℝ) n S x) (hmn : m + 1 ≤ n) :
    ContMDiffAt (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) 𝓘(ℝ, StrongDual ℝ A) m (familyFiberDeriv S) x := by
  -- The fibre derivative is the Fréchet derivative of `S` in its vector-space factor.
  rw [funext (familyFiberDeriv_eq_fderiv S)]
  exact hS.fderiv_right (g := Function.curry S) hmn

/-- The fibre derivative of a `C^n` generating family is `C^m` when `m + 1 ≤ n`. -/
theorem contMDiff_familyFiberDeriv [IsManifold I 1 M] {m n : WithTop ℕ∞}
    (hS : ContMDiff (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) 𝓘(ℝ) n S) (hmn : m + 1 ≤ n) :
    ContMDiff (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) 𝓘(ℝ, StrongDual ℝ A) m (familyFiberDeriv S) :=
  fun x ↦ contMDiffAt_familyFiberDeriv (hS x) hmn

/-- **The differential of the fibre derivative.** For a generating family `S` on `M × A`, with `M`
a boundaryless `C²` manifold, which is `C²` at `x = (q, a)`, the differential at `x` of the fibre
derivative, applied to a tangent vector `v = (w, c)` and then to `b ∈ A`, is
`d_a (d_q S) b w + D²_a S c b`: the mixed Hessian of `S` in `w`, plus the second derivative of
`S(q, ·)` in `c`. -/
theorem mvfderiv_familyFiberDeriv_apply [IsManifold I 2 M] [I.Boundaryless] {x : M × A}
    (hS : ContMDiffAt (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) 𝓘(ℝ) 2 S x)
    (v : TangentSpace (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) x) (b : A) :
    mvfderiv (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) (familyFiberDeriv S) x v b =
      mixedHessian I 𝓘(ℝ, A) S x b v.1 + fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ fun a ↦ S (x.1, a)) x.2 v.2 b := by
  have hF := (contMDiffAt_familyFiberDeriv (m := 1) hS (by norm_num)).mdifferentiableAt
    one_ne_zero
  rw [hF.mvfderiv_prod_eq_add_apply, add_apply]
  congr 1
  · -- Differentiating `∂_a S` in the base direction is the mixed Hessian of the swapped family.
    rw [← mixedHessian_comp_swap_apply hS (v.1 : TangentSpace I x.1) b, mixedHessian_def]
    simp only [familyFiberDeriv_def, Function.comp_apply, Prod.swap_prod_mk, Prod.fst_swap,
      Prod.snd_swap]
  · simp only [familyFiberDeriv_eq_fderiv]
    exact DFunLike.congr_fun (mvfderiv_eq_fderiv_apply (𝕜 := ℝ) _ _ v.2) b

variable [IsManifold I ∞ M] [I.Boundaryless]

/-- At a point where the differential of the fibre derivative of a smooth generating family `S`
is surjective, a tangent vector killed by it and by the differential of the source projection
`(q, a) ↦ (q, d_q S)` is zero. -/
private theorem eq_zero_of_mfderiv_generatingSource_eq_zero
    (hS : ContMDiff (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ S) {x : M × A}
    (hsurj : Function.Surjective (mvfderiv (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) (familyFiberDeriv S) x))
    {u : TangentSpace (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) x}
    (hu : mvfderiv (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) (familyFiberDeriv S) x u = 0)
    (hιu : mfderiv (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, E →L[ℝ] ℝ)) (generatingSource I S) x u = 0) :
    u = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨w, b⟩ := u
  -- The source projection lies over the first projection, so the base component vanishes.
  have hw : w = 0 := by
    have h : ContinuousLinearMap.fst ℝ E (E →L[ℝ] ℝ)
        (mfderiv (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, E →L[ℝ] ℝ)) (generatingSource I S) x (w, b)) = w :=
      DFunLike.congr_fun (fst_comp_mfderiv_generatingSource hS x) (w, b)
    rw [hιu] at h
    -- The zero tangent vector is the zero of the model space `E × E'`.
    exact h.symm.trans rfl
  subst hw
  -- On the vertical vector `(0, b)` the source projection is the mixed Hessian, which kills `b`.
  have hH : mixedHessian I 𝓘(ℝ, A) S x b = 0 := by
    have h : mfderiv (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, E →L[ℝ] ℝ)) (generatingSource I S) x (0, b) =
        ((0 : E), mixedHessian I 𝓘(ℝ, A) S x b) :=
      DFunLike.congr_fun (mfderiv_generatingSource_comp_inr hS x) b
    rw [hιu] at h
    exact (congrArg Prod.snd h).symm
  -- The second derivative of `S(q, ·)` in the direction `b` vanishes, by the hypothesis on
  -- `(0, b)`.
  have hb (c : A) : fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ fun a ↦ S (x.1, a)) x.2 b c = 0 := by
    have h := mvfderiv_familyFiberDeriv_apply ((hS x).of_le (by simp)) (0, b) c
    rw [hu, map_zero, zero_apply, zero_add] at h
    exact h.symm
  -- Hence every covector in the range of the differential of `∂_a S`, which is all of `A'`,
  -- vanishes on `b`, using the symmetry of the second derivative of `S(q, ·)`.
  have hsymm : IsSymmSndFDerivAt ℝ (fun a ↦ S (x.1, a)) x.2 :=
    (contMDiff_iff_contDiff.mp (hS.comp (contMDiff_const.prodMk contMDiff_id))).contDiffAt
      |>.isSymmSndFDerivAt (by simp)
  refine Prod.ext rfl (SeparatingDual.eq_zero_of_forall_dual_eq_zero (R := ℝ) fun β ↦ ?_)
  obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := hsurj β
  rw [mvfderiv_familyFiberDeriv_apply ((hS x).of_le (by simp)) v b, hH, zero_apply, zero_add,
    hsymm]
  exact hb v.2

/-! ### The fibre-critical set as a manifold -/

section CriticalSet

variable [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ A]

/-- The fibre-critical set has the dimension of the base: `dim (E × A) - dim A' = dim E`. -/
private theorem finrank_prod_sub_finrank_strongDual :
    finrank ℝ (E × A) - finrank ℝ (StrongDual ℝ A) = finrank ℝ E := by
  rw [finrank_prod, ContinuousLinearMap.dual_finrank_eq]
  omega

/-- The fibre-critical set has half the dimension of `T*M`: `2 dim E = dim (E × E')`. -/
private theorem two_mul_finrank_fin_eq_finrank_prod_strongDual :
    2 * finrank ℝ (Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) = finrank ℝ (E × (E →L[ℝ] ℝ)) := by
  rw [finrank_fin_fun, finrank_prod, ContinuousLinearMap.dual_finrank_eq, two_mul]

variable (hS : ContMDiff (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) 𝓘(ℝ) ∞ S)
  (hreg : IsRegularValue (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) 𝓘(ℝ, StrongDual ℝ A) (familyFiberDeriv S) 0)

/-- The **fibre-critical set** `{x | ∂_a S x = 0}` of a smooth generating family `S : M × A → ℝ`,
with `M` boundaryless and `M` and `A` finite-dimensional, which is transverse, that is, for which
`0` is a regular value of the fibre derivative, as a charted space modelled on `Fin (dim M) → ℝ`:
it is a regular level of the fibre derivative, with the atlas of
`TauCeti.regularLevelChartedSpace`. -/
@[instance_reducible]
def familyCriticalSetChartedSpace :
    ChartedSpace (Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0} :=
  regularLevelChartedSpace (fun x _ ↦ contMDiffAt_familyFiberDeriv (hS x) (by simp)) hreg
    finrank_prod_sub_finrank_strongDual

/-- The fibre-critical set of a smooth transverse generating family on `M × A`, with `M`
boundaryless and `M` and `A` finite-dimensional, is a smooth manifold of the dimension of `M`. -/
theorem isManifold_familyCriticalSet :
    letI := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
    IsManifold 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) ∞ {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0} :=
  isManifold_regularLevel (by simp)
    (fun x _ ↦ contMDiff_familyFiberDeriv (m := ∞) hS (by simp) x) hreg
    finrank_prod_sub_finrank_strongDual

/-- The fibre-critical set of a smooth transverse generating family on `M × A`, with `M`
boundaryless and `M` and `A` finite-dimensional, is a smoothly embedded submanifold of `M × A`. -/
theorem isSmoothEmbedding_coe_familyCriticalSet :
    letI := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
    IsSmoothEmbedding 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) ∞
      (Subtype.val : {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → M × A) :=
  isSmoothEmbedding_coe_regularLevel (by simp)
    (fun x _ ↦ contMDiff_familyFiberDeriv (m := ∞) hS (by simp) x) hreg
    finrank_prod_sub_finrank_strongDual

/-- For a smooth transverse generating family on `M × A`, with `M` boundaryless and `M` and `A`
finite-dimensional, the tangent space of the fibre-critical set at `z` is the kernel of the
differential of the fibre derivative there. -/
theorem range_mfderiv_coe_familyCriticalSet (z : {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0}) :
    letI := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
    (mfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A))
      (Subtype.val : {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → M × A) z).range =
      (mfderiv (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) 𝓘(ℝ, StrongDual ℝ A) (familyFiberDeriv S) z).ker :=
  range_mfderiv_coe_regularLevel _ hreg _ z

/-- **The Liouville form pulls back to the differential of `S`.** The source projection
`ι_S (q, a) = (q, d_q S)` of a smooth transverse generating family `S` on `M × A`, with `M`
boundaryless and `M` and `A` finite-dimensional, pulls the Liouville form of `T*M` back along the
inclusion of the fibre-critical set to the differential of the restriction of `S`. -/
theorem mpullback_generatingSource_comp_coe_liouvilleForm :
    letI := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
    mpullback 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, E →L[ℝ] ℝ))
        (generatingSource I S ∘ (Subtype.val : {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → M × A))
        (liouvilleForm I M).1 =
      mextDeriv (RoughForm.ofFunction 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ)
        (S ∘ (Subtype.val : {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → M × A))) := by
  let _ := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
  have hj := (isSmoothEmbedding_coe_familyCriticalSet hS hreg).contMDiff
  funext z
  ext v
  have hSz : MDifferentiableAt (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) 𝓘(ℝ) S z.1 := (hS z.1).mdifferentiableAt (by simp)
  have hjz := (hj z).mdifferentiableAt (n := ∞) (by simp)
  rw [mpullback_liouvilleForm_apply_of_proj_comp_eq (ψ := generatingSource I S ∘ Subtype.val)
      (g := Prod.fst ∘ Subtype.val)
      (fun y ↦ proj_generatingSource (I := I) (S := S) y.1)
      (((contMDiff_generatingSource hS).comp hj z).mdifferentiableAt (by simp)),
    mextDeriv_ofFunction, ContinuousAlternatingMap.ofSubsingleton_apply_apply,
    mvfderiv_comp_apply_of_eq z hSz hjz rfl, hSz.mvfderiv_prod_eq_add_apply,
    mfderiv_comp_apply z mdifferentiableAt_fst hjz, mfderiv_fst]
  -- The auxiliary component of `dS` is the fibre derivative, which vanishes on the critical set.
  -- The ascription reads `∂_a S z = 0`, an equation in `A'`, on the tangent space of `A`, which is
  -- `A` itself. The goal is not type-correct at implicit transparency, so `rw` and `simp` cannot
  -- evaluate the zero covector after rewriting with `familyFiberDeriv_def` there.
  have h0 : mvfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, A) (fun a ↦ S (z.1.1, a)) z.1.2 = 0 :=
    (familyFiberDeriv_def S z.1).symm.trans z.2
  rw [h0]
  -- What remains is the base component of `dS`, which is the covector of the source projection.
  exact (DFunLike.congr_fun (generatingSource_snd (I := I) (S := S) z.1)
    (mfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) Subtype.val z (v 0)).1).trans
      (add_zero _).symm

/-- The source projection is smooth along the fibre-critical set. -/
private theorem contMDiff_generatingSource_comp_coe :
    letI := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
    ContMDiff 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, E →L[ℝ] ℝ)) ∞
      (generatingSource I S ∘ (Subtype.val : {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → M × A)) :=
  letI := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
  (contMDiff_generatingSource hS).comp (isSmoothEmbedding_coe_familyCriticalSet hS hreg).contMDiff

/-- The source projection has injective differentials along the fibre-critical set. -/
private theorem injective_mfderiv_generatingSource_comp_coe
    (z : {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0}) :
    letI := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
    Function.Injective (mfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, E →L[ℝ] ℝ))
      (generatingSource I S ∘ (Subtype.val : {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → M × A))
      z) := by
  let _ := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
  have := isManifold_familyCriticalSet hS hreg
  have hj := isSmoothEmbedding_coe_familyCriticalSet hS hreg
  have hjz := (hj.contMDiff z).mdifferentiableAt (n := ∞) (by simp)
  rw [mfderiv_comp z ((contMDiff_generatingSource hS z.1).mdifferentiableAt (by simp)) hjz]
  intro v w hvw
  rw [ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply, ContinuousLinearMap.comp_apply] at hvw
  refine hj.isImmersion.mfderiv_injective (by simp) z (sub_eq_zero.mp ?_)
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective (mvfderiv (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) (familyFiberDeriv S) z.1) :=
    isRegularPoint_iff_surjective_mvfderiv.mp (hreg.isRegularPoint z.2)
  -- Vectors tangent to the critical set lie in the kernel of the differential of `∂_a S`.
  have hker (v' : TangentSpace 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) z) :
      mvfderiv (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) (familyFiberDeriv S) z.1
        (mfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) Subtype.val z v') = 0 := by
    have h : mfderiv 𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) Subtype.val z v' ∈
        (mvfderiv (I.prod 𝓘(ℝ, A)) (familyFiberDeriv S) z.1).ker := by
      rw [ker_mvfderiv, ← range_mfderiv_coe_familyCriticalSet hS hreg z]
      exact ⟨v', rfl⟩
    rwa [LinearMap.mem_ker, ContinuousLinearMap.coe_coe] at h
  refine eq_zero_of_mfderiv_generatingSource_eq_zero hS hsurj ?_ ?_
  · rw [map_sub, hker v, hker w, sub_zero]
  · rw [map_sub, hvw, sub_self]

/-- **The fibre-critical set of a generating family is an exact Lagrangian map.** Let `S` be a
smooth generating family on `M × A`, with `M` boundaryless and `M` and `A` finite-dimensional,
which is transverse: `0` is a regular value of its fibre derivative `∂_a S`. With its manifold
structure as a regular level, the fibre-critical set maps to `T*M` by
`ι_S (q, a) = (q, d_q S(q, a))` as an exact Lagrangian map for the canonical symplectic form
`ω = -dλ` and its primitive `λ`, with primitive the restriction of `S`. -/
theorem isExactLagrangianMap_generatingSource_comp_coe :
    letI := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
    (isSymplectic_symplecticForm (I := I) (M := M)).isNondegenerate.IsExactLagrangianMap
      𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ) (liouvilleForm I M)
      (generatingSource I S ∘ (Subtype.val : {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → M × A))
      (S ∘ (Subtype.val : {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → M × A)) := by
  let _ := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
  have := isManifold_familyCriticalSet hS hreg
  refine (SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.isExactLagrangianMap_iff_of_finrank
    symplecticForm_eq_neg_mextDerivₗ (contMDiff_generatingSource_comp_coe hS hreg)
    (injective_mfderiv_generatingSource_comp_coe hS hreg)
    two_mul_finrank_fin_eq_finrank_prod_strongDual).mpr
    ⟨hS.comp (isSmoothEmbedding_coe_familyCriticalSet hS hreg).contMDiff,
      mpullback_generatingSource_comp_coe_liouvilleForm hS hreg⟩

/-- **The fibre-critical set of a generating family is a Lagrangian immersion.** For a smooth
transverse generating family `S` on `M × A`, with `M` boundaryless and `M` and `A`
finite-dimensional, the source projection `ι_S (q, a) = (q, d_q S(q, a))` restricted to the
fibre-critical set `{∂_a S = 0}` is a Lagrangian immersion into `T*M`. Its image need not be
embedded. -/
theorem isLagrangianImmersion_generatingSource_comp_coe :
    letI := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
    (isSymplectic_symplecticForm (I := I) (M := M)).isNondegenerate.IsLagrangianImmersion
      𝓘(ℝ, Fin (finrank ℝ E) → ℝ)
      (generatingSource I S ∘ (Subtype.val : {x : M × A // familyFiberDeriv S x = 0} → M × A)) :=
  letI := familyCriticalSetChartedSpace hS hreg
  haveI := isManifold_familyCriticalSet hS hreg
  ⟨(contMDiff_generatingSource_comp_coe hS hreg).isImmersion_of_injective_mfderiv (by simp)
      (injective_mfderiv_generatingSource_comp_coe hS hreg),
    (isExactLagrangianMap_generatingSource_comp_coe hS hreg).isLagrangianMap.isIsotropicMap,
    two_mul_finrank_fin_eq_finrank_prod_strongDual⟩

